282
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,500
卢克:听着,我不明白你干嘛这么生我的气.
Luke: Listen, I don't know why you're so mad at me.

283
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:28,320
迈克说我什么也没做错.
Mike said I wasn't doing anything wrong.

284
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:33,160
本:迈克?你告诉他你怎么对我了?
Ben: Mike?You told him to do this to me?

285
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:36,340
迈克:本,你能安静会吗?我还想吃鸡呢.
Mike: Ben, would you keep it down?I'm trying to enjoy my chicken here.

286
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,740
本:哦.你这么喜欢吃饭?你可以吃我的.
Ben: Oh, you like dinner so much?You can have some of mine.

287
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:38,840
大家:(叫喊)嘿!你俩住嘴!
Entire family: (yelling) Hey!Stop it you two!

288
00:15:39,660 --> 00:15:41,260
杰森: 你们几个怎么了?
Jason: What's going on between you guys?

289
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:42,880
迈克:你说你为什么要扔我?
Mike: What are you throwing food at me for?

290
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:44,300
本:对不起,抱歉.我不是故意扔你的.我是想扔他!
Ben: I'm sorry, excuse me.I didn't mean to throw food at Mike.I meant to throw it at him!

291
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:46,200
大家:(叫喊)别吵了!
Entire family: (yelling)

292
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:50,560
麦琪:我说了,住嘴!
Maggie: I said stop it!

293
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,880
杰森:出去,出去,
Jason: Get out of here!All you guys!

294
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,460
都出去.你也出去,迈克,
And you go with them, since you obviously have something to do with this,

295
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:56,860
很明显你准与这事有关.真没有想到.
Mike.Big surprise!

296
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:03,260
克莉丝:不能不走吗?我还从来没看过打食物仗呢.
Chrissy: Can't they stay?I've never seen a food fight before.

297
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:06,500
杰森:你乖乖的坐着,吃你的鸡和蘑菇.
Jason: You just stay here and eat your chicken and fungus.

298
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,600
迈克:算了吧,本,我们觉得你对谢丽尔并没有兴趣.
Mike: C'mon, Ben.We didn't think you were interested in Cheryl.

299
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:14,840
本:这并不意味着我想让这臭小子把她偷走!
Ben: That didn't mean I wanted her stolen away by some sniveling weasel.

300
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,880
卢克:是的,好吧,我这臭小子要教训你下.
Luke: Yeah, well, this sniveling weasel's gonna pop you one.

301
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:16,980
本:什么?
Ben: Yeah?

302
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,460
迈克:嘿,嘿,嘿,伙计们,伙计们,得了吧.你们为个姑娘打架,
Mike: Hey, hey, hey, guys, guys, c'mon.You're fighting over a girl.

303
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:21,700
好吧,为什么不省省为什么重要的事干一架呢?比如…谁掌握遥控器.
All right, now why don't you save it for the important stuff, like...who gets the remote control.

304
00:16:25,060 --> 00:16:28,360
本:这事儿也算上;他为什么总是霸着遥控器.
Ben: That's another thing; how come he gets the remote control all the time?

305
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,600
卢克:什么?那在你的脸上换频道会怎么样?
Luke: Yeah?How would you like the channels changed on your face?

306
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:32,640
迈克:嘿,嘿,嘿,
Mike: Hey, hey, hey, guy, guys, knock it off.

307
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,020
伙计们,伙计们,别吵了.好吧,
All right now, Luke, c'mon,

308
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,700
卢克,你先上楼去,我跟本好好聊一会.
go upstairs and give me a minute to figure this out with Ben.

309
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:40,060
卢克:好的.我得去把自己耳朵里的土豆泥弄出来.
Luke: Sure, I gotta go Q-tip the mashed potatoes out of my ear.

310
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:45,020
迈克:好了,本,你介意告诉我发生什么事了吗?
Mike: Now, Ben, you mind telling me what's going on here?

311
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,700
本:谢丽尔爱慕我.她拜倒在神圣的本的脚下.
Ben: Cheryl adored me.She worshipped at the shrine o'Ben.

312
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:51,000
迈克:哦,行了.你觉得这公平吗,利用姑娘的崇拜来满足自己的虚荣心?
Mike: Oh, now, c'mon.Do you think that's really fair?To use some girl like that to stroke your own ego?

313
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:55,200
本:当然了.
Ben: Of course.

314
00:16:56,220 --> 00:17:01,360
迈克:本,如果有个姑娘也这样对你呢?哦,很抱歉我这么说.我的头发没白吧?
Mike: Ben, what if some girl was doing the same thing to you?Oh, I'm sorry about that.How is my hair?

315
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:09,560
本:迈克,她让我感到自己很重要.
Ben: Mike, she made me feel important.

316
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:12,200
长期以来,
I mean, all my life I've been Seaver's little brother.

317
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:14,120
我都是西沃的小弟弟.大家都这么叫我.
I mean, that's all I ever heard.

318
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:17,480
我总算走出了你的阴影,现在却又和卢克搅在一起.
I'm finally out of your shadow, and now I'm the kid who lives with Luke.

319
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:21,100
我是说,他的成绩比我好,
I mean, he gets better grades than me, looks better in my clothes,

320
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:22,980
穿上我的衣服比我帅,我还要吃他喜欢的蘑菇.
and I choke on his mushrooms.

321
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:27,080
他甚至偷走了你该给我的建议.你是我哥哥,
He's even stealing the advice you should be giving me.

322
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:29,640
不是卢克的.
You're my brother, not Luke's!

323
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:41,600
克莉丝:嘿!
Chrissy: Hi!

324
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,080
杰森和麦琪:嘿,宝贝!
Jason and Maggie: Hi, Honey!

325
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:49,000
麦琪:课上的怎么样?你把我们的工作告诉他们了吗?
Maggie: How was school?Did you tell them about our jobs.

326
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:51,820
克莉丝:是的!太棒了!我还画了画呢.
Chrissy: Yeah!It was great.I even drew pictures.

327
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,020
杰森:哦,真不错.
Jason: Oh, how nice.

328
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:54,280
麦琪:你真有想像力.
Maggie: That's very imaginative.

329
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:57,560
克莉丝:对,太棒了.
Chrissy: Yeah, it was great.First I told them what daddy does.

330
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,360
我先说了爸爸的工作.我说,他把女人带进他的办公室,
I said he takes women into his office,

331
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:03,160
关上门,让她们躺在睡椅上.
closes the door and makes them lay on the couch.

332
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:07,020
一小时后,她们哭着出来,还给他钱.
An hour later they come out crying and give him money.

333
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:11,300
麦琪:那你是怎么说我的工作的?
Maggie: And what did you tell them about my job?

334
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:15,820
克莉丝:我说你的工作比爸爸有趣的多.你喜欢一遍又一遍地咬男人的平头短裤.因为我知道你喜欢"快乐男士"牌短裤.
Chrissy: I said that you have way more fun than daddy.I said that you

335
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:19,500
love to snap men's boxer shorts.Over and over.Cause you like a happy man

336
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:21,200
麦琪:哈-哈.
Maggie: Oh-oh.

337
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:26,900
克莉丝:我还说,结束后你往短裤上面倒热咖啡.
Chrissy: And I said when you finish, you pour hot coffee on them.

338
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:32,080
杰森:那么,你老师认为你的报告怎么样?
Jason: Well, what did your teacher think of this report?

339
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:33,580
克莉丝:她肯定很喜欢;她让我直接回家,
Chrissy: She must have liked it;

340
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:36,080
让你们给她打个电话.
she told me to go straight home and have you call her.

341
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,540
克莉丝:对,现在就给她打电话,好吗?(门铃声)
Jason: Yeah, why don't we do that right now.[Doorbell]

342
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,560
谢丽尔:嘿,本在家吗?
Cheryl: Hi, is Ben home?

343
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:51,160
杰森:是的,快进来.本!
Jason: Yeah, come on in.Ben!

344
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:58,680
本:谢丽尔,真是个惊喜.
Ben: Cheryl, what a pleasant surprise.

345
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:01,180
谢丽尔:我是来还你历史笔记本的,
Cheryl: I just came here to drop off your history notes,

346
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:03,140
因为我们不会在一起写作业了.
since we won't be doing our presentation together.

347
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,240
本:你在说什么呀?我们是学习对子啊.
Ben: What are you talking about?We're partners.

348
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:06,460
谢丽尔:不再是了.
Cheryl: Not anymore.

349
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:11,420
本:谢丽尔,我们的关系怎么了?
Ben: Cheryl, what happened to our relationship that let an outsider come

350
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:12,240
怎么让外人插进来呢?
between us?

351
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:16,080
谢丽尔:你从不打电话,从不约我,还在学校作弄我!
Cheryl: You never called, we never went out, and you made fun of me at school.

352
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:18,280
本:嘿,你不是在找茬吧.
Ben: Sure, if you want to nitpick.

353
00:19:19,940 --> 00:19:21,560
不过,我们可以像过去一样相处.
But we can make things the way they used to be.

354
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:23,000
谢丽尔:像过去一样相处?
Cheryl: The way they used to be?

355
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,400
我在你的更衣箱前转悠,为你做作业,
Me hanging around your locker, doing your homework,

356
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:29,020
希望你能和我一起吃一顿午饭?
hoping that just once you'd eat lunch with me?

357
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:30,480
本:我没意见.
Ben: Worked for me.

358
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:35,980
谢丽尔:算了!这不会让你喜欢我的.
Cheryl: Forget it!It didn't make you like me.

359
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:37,100
知道吗?我对自己都不满意.
And you know, I didn't like me either.

360
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:42,280
就算卢克对我没兴趣,
Luke may not be interested in me,

361
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:44,760
事情也不会回到过去那个样子了.
but things are never going back to the way they were.

362
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:51,440
本:等等!,等一会儿,你是什么意思,卢克对你没兴趣?
Ben: Wait!Wait a minute.What do you mean; Luke's not interested in you?

363
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:53,420
谢丽尔:问他好了;他取消了约会.
Cheryl: Ask him; he broke our date.

364
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:54,980
本:是吗?为什么?
Ben: He did?Why?

365
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:57,560
谢丽尔:他说,因为什么家庭问题.
Cheryl: He said something about family problems.

366
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:03,540
本:听我说,谢丽尔,
Ben: Look, Cheryl, I've been a jerk and I'm sorry.

367
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:06,160
我是个傻瓜,我很抱歉.你愿意到厨房等我一会吗?
Would you mind going in the kitchen for a minute?

368
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:08,020
谢丽尔:为什么?你想让我给你做饭吗?
Cheryl: Why?Do you want me to fix you dinner?

369
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:13,260
本:就待一会,求你了.(喊)卢克!
Ben: Just for a minute, please.(yelling) Luke!

370
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,240
卢克:你喊什么?
Luke: You bellowed?

371
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,560
本:我说,你跟谢丽尔怎么了?
Ben: Listen.What happened between you and Cheryl?

372
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:25,080
卢克:没什么.没发生什么啊?
Luke: Nothing happened.Nothing's going to happen.

373
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,920
本:但我听你说过你真的喜欢她.
Ben: But I thought you said you really liked her.

374
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:31,100
卢克:是的,不过,
Luke: Yeah, but I didn't know you'd get so freaked.

375
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:34,660
我没想到,你会这么生气.而且,
And besides, you and your family have been so good to me,

376
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:36,840
你和全家对我这么好,我不能以怨报德.
this isn't how I wanted to repay you.

377
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:38,220
回头见.
See you around.

378
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:42,520
本:卢克,我们不需要你报答.我们希望你留在这儿.
Ben: Luke, we don't need you to repay us.You know, we want you here.

379
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,400
卢克:以前我领教过这种事.有一天,
Luke: I've seen it happen to kids before.

380
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,940
你做的太过分了,就成了不受欢迎的人.
One day you just go too far and wear out your welcome.

381
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:51,540
本:要是这样的话,开萝尔早就被赶出家门了.
Ben: If that were true, Carol'd have been gone a long time ago.

382
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:59,260
卢克:以前我们可从没为蘑菇和毛衣吵过架.
Luke: Well, we never did fight over mushrooms and sweaters before.

383
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:10,000
本:听我说,我决不和陌生人这样吵的.只有对惹我生气的兄弟,我才会这样.
Ben: Look, I'd never fight like that with a stranger.Only a brother...who really ticks me off.

384
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:17,700
卢克:我也是这样的.
Luke: The feeling's mutual.

385
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:23,100
本:好了,既然我们还得在一起相处下去,那你愿不愿意帮我个忙?
Ben: Well, since it looks like we're both gonna be here awhile, would you mind doing me a favor?

386
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:23,800
卢克:当然了.
Luke: Sure.

387
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,960
本:去看看我的"历史作业",就在厨房里.
Ben: Go check out my history presentation.It's in the kitchen.

388
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,800
卢克:你的历史作业?
Luke: Your history presentation?

389
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:33,840
本:快去吧,你嘴里一股蘑菇味.
Ben: Just get in there, mushroom-breath!

390
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:37,900
谢丽尔:卢克.
Cheryl: Luke.

391
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:40,000
卢克:谢丽尔.
Luke: Cheryl.

392
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,980
谢丽尔:听着,我…我还是走吧.
Cheryl: Listen, I...I'd better go.

393
00:21:45,260 --> 00:21:46,960
卢克:不,不,不.你别走.我走.
Luke: No, no, no.You can stay; I'll go.

394
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,340
谢丽尔:不,不,不.你别走.
Cheryl: No, no, no.You can stay.

395
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:48,440
卢克:不,不,不.我走.
Luke: No, no, no.I'm going.

396
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:51,600
谢丽尔:卢克,你住在这里啊.
Cheryl: Luke, you live here.

397
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:52,700
卢克:哦.
Luke: Oh.

398
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:57,740
谢丽尔:那么,再见.
Cheryl: Well, see ya.

399
00:21:57,740 --> 00:21:59,280
卢克:我说,谢丽尔.
Luke: Look, Cheryl.

400
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,660
我有两个解决方案.一是我可以三年之内不理你,直到你发疯地想我;
There's two ways I can play this; I can spend the next three years ignoring

401
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:06,740
you until you're crazed with desire for me

402
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:12,900
或者第二个方案-我这就邀请你参加赛蒂霍金斯舞会.
or plan B - I could ask you here and now to the Sadie Hawkins dance.

403
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:22,200
谢丽尔:不,你不能.应该是我邀请你.好吧,5个字:赛蒂霍金斯.
Cheryl: No, you can't.I'm supposed to ask you.Okay, two words.Sadie.Hawkins.

404
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:25,000
卢克:一个字:好.
谢丽尔和卢克:噢-噢-噢!
00:22:25,000
Luke: One word.Yes. Cheryl and Luke: Woo-hoo-hoo!
